d #edb/ref 17592186571978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3065f6cb-298c-5d20-ac8b-5527933c3f44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571619} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b587d3b-55bf-5b89-b2c4-ae91f0538308" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571988}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "52f19af3-7870-568c-aad1-0f002a1758f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-69951" :question/problem "![](images/31/314cd1d2e150c078fa7232c81125de44fb8c26c176d2a1f32ab02fbae2eef299.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\mathbf{m}=-\\mathbf{g}$\n\nII. $\\mathbf{a}=\\mathbf{z}$\n\nIII. $\\mathbf{g}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{m}$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. The magnitude of $m$ is greater than the magnitude of $g.$ So, $m\\ne -g.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $a$ and $z$ have opposite directions. So, $a\\ne z.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, vectors $g$ and $m$ are parallel and have opposite directions. Also the magnitude of $g$ is $\\frac{1}{2}$ times the magnitude of $m.$ So, $g=-\\frac{1}{2}m.$\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b86a3d8-bbdc-510c-bdb1-25822dde58a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571647} {:answer/id #uuid "b55d5c71-dfbf-5d5c-b477-04b04d7dda95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571856} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ff3248-4b13-5d5b-9c41-dfbe5793add0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571900} {:answer/id #uuid "cdea4944-bf33-5ba6-9d6a-697b65a617dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571909} {:answer/id #uuid "d66f4a36-7bf8-5c75-8d2c-1dec7887829a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdea4944-bf33-5ba6-9d6a-697b65a617dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571909} :answer-field/id #uuid "471634b7-feb0-50b9-9eda-91e81c3b2ea0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572013}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f081ecc9-be21-500f-81d8-5fe5809e98ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-76939" :question/problem "![](images/92/9236e136f26433023d806181fcfbef9c05d4976f75e14f74840ae7f48a35da99.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\mathbf{r}=3\\mathbf{q}$\n\nII. $\\mathbf{s}=2\\mathbf{t}$\n\nIII. $\\mathbf{p}=-\\mathbf{s}$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. The vectors $r$ and $q$ have the opposite directions. So, $r\\ne 3q.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, vectors $s$ and $t$ are parallel and have the same directions. Also, the magnitude of $s$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $t.$ So, $s=2t.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The vectors $p$ and $s$ are parallel and have the opposite directions. Also, their magnitudes are the same. So, $p=-s.$\n\nTherefore, statements II and III are true, and statement I is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186628577 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1acb6bf3-d37f-5ec3-a852-0e187ac4aaae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628580} {:answer/id #uuid "51fbc6a2-1582-5821-85ab-2ed4824f45ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628587} {:answer/id #uuid "5afb4d71-23ee-58fb-b91d-d4d9423224b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628588} {:answer/id #uuid "621b0c1b-48b6-5745-b28f-0f0b0f523edf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628590} {:answer/id #uuid "e2da1981-de26-52ad-a1f0-f974f40de758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5afb4d71-23ee-58fb-b91d-d4d9423224b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628588} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffafce5d-c424-5f68-98d1-a2fa8eab6c87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628617}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "108e47f5-c29f-5489-ac87-ae2bfab072a3" :question/problem "![](images/cc/cce654debb192f5f2ef24c33a7fc32d545eab47a5e4b718a2ea82e314cf812c8.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $s=3t$\n\nII. $r=2p$\n\nIII. $q=-r$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. The vectors $s$ and $t$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $s$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $t$. So, $s\\ne 3t$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The vectors $r$ and $p$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $r$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $p$. So, $r=2p$.\n\n- Statement III is false. The vectors $q$ and $r$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $q$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $r$. So, $q\\ne -r$.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186628583 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "812e2bcc-c146-58d7-8367-4c919e3086c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628597} {:answer/id #uuid "972190c2-6bac-5ce1-b6f0-f8dde8d5a799" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "972190c2-6bac-5ce1-b6f0-f8dde8d5a799" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628601} :answer-field/id #uuid "8792e7e9-419a-5266-b478-5ecdc6c82b4b" :answer-field/key "$d=2e$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628599} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e842bed5-351a-5507-a705-f2e2bd9d1798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628612} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ea9cfb-d1f4-5e9c-9578-b24cba66a134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e842bed5-351a-5507-a705-f2e2bd9d1798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628612} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5de8833-2497-500f-931c-49c677cc2aea" :answer-field/key "$a=-b$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628605} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca5e1234-f631-5013-b8fa-42722b9fe5ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628607} {:answer/id #uuid "d1af3295-ece5-531e-8880-9ab230307deb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1af3295-ece5-531e-8880-9ab230307deb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628609} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff2dedd4-28e1-5848-a30b-a9b650dbc289" :answer-field/key "$d=-2e$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628616}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f3a2b79-75e1-5091-907c-0c44e8f36d34" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7b1496185812c5663cf8e07b02a8e51f9c3b07393d4c08d988cbf1fcd3179a06.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is true. The vectors $d$ and $e$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $d$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $e$. So, $d=-2e$.\n\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $a$ and $b$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $a$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $b$. So, $a\\ne -b$.\n\n- Statement III is false. The vectors $d$ and $e$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $d$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $e$. So, $d\\ne 2e$.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186628589 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b8dfad6-c081-53b4-aaa0-2e834483cc46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628586} {:answer/id #uuid "6df7ba2d-a2db-5442-b586-0e76962bcc46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6df7ba2d-a2db-5442-b586-0e76962bcc46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628592} :answer-field/id #uuid "27cc2e80-c5bb-53e5-8327-20592dc86c6e" :answer-field/key "$b=-\\frac{1}{2}d$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628582} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a76f318-9136-5ad7-a463-aa64f570a28c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628579} {:answer/id #uuid "dd62623f-e10f-59e5-82de-e1b025bb8248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd62623f-e10f-59e5-82de-e1b025bb8248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628610} :answer-field/id #uuid "6867fa8d-25eb-5c06-a45e-330141e360cd" :answer-field/key "$a=e$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628591} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "403938a3-9935-53ed-bd80-1df23fc797d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628584} {:answer/id #uuid "af92a61b-92f1-5f91-83c1-7c6752a3458b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af92a61b-92f1-5f91-83c1-7c6752a3458b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628604} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc6ba19f-647e-5cb0-ab75-03ba29feb426" :answer-field/key "$d=-b$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628606}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5edf6afc-78ce-5695-b6e3-1a33f6ac3097" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b6c26d5365880d39ef1e5170dbfad0632ca60735727a6779b20059f7b18e8687.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. The vectors $d$ and $b$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $d$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $b$. So, $d\\ne -b$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The vectors $b$ and $d$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $b$ is $\\frac{1}{2}$ times the magnitude of $d$. So, $b=-\\frac{1}{2}d$.\n\n- Statement III is false. The vectors $a$ and $e$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $a$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $e$. So, $a\\ne e$.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186628594 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "794da91f-723c-5590-b235-67d7005fbeaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628593} {:answer/id #uuid "7f863861-129d-5963-b3a9-3fa2294f8978" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628595} {:answer/id #uuid "80b1864b-7947-54ef-90b9-4982b447a2fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628596} {:answer/id #uuid "9f7b4c01-27ac-54ff-a091-389aa6d8cbcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628602} {:answer/id #uuid "cb5f5624-fdfe-5e90-9150-b1872ea07148" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628608}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb5f5624-fdfe-5e90-9150-b1872ea07148" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628608} :answer-field/id #uuid "8417fba8-92a0-5d30-8475-2df3d791c2cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628598}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "79a05414-7032-5178-a92c-c08b89d2f3cd" :question/problem "![](images/7a/7ad3dd07f782811a42c9e0b06299a95c4d0ce984bdbdabd5f952ef0f6820155f.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $a=-z$\n\nII. $m=k$\n\nIII. $z=-\\frac{1}{2}a$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. The vectors $a$ and $z$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $a$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $z$. So, $a\\ne -z$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The vectors $m$ and $k$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $m$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $k$. So, $m=k$.\n\n- Statement III is false. The vectors $z$ and $a$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $z$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $a$. So, $z\\ne -\\frac{1}{2}a$.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186628603 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19dbc5e2-305b-56d2-977a-01ec8053b29c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628578} {:answer/id #uuid "1f7dea34-2eb3-5394-bc4c-ce9ccccda263" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628581} {:answer/id #uuid "8cb087b0-2225-5159-8fb1-25c98e9128a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628600} {:answer/id #uuid "e997689c-5678-5f00-a4db-d0f7367a8d1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628613} {:answer/id #uuid "ef0777be-960b-5991-9242-395252a2b036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cb087b0-2225-5159-8fb1-25c98e9128a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628600} :answer-field/id #uuid "411ada06-786f-5ee8-bc0d-900b4cf4067c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628585}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a98b3fb4-9dbe-550d-8f88-85d63dacb822" :question/problem "![](images/b4/b4a29b1ca13d5ddcb342f247b8b477058586bdad0bb4a6af588d66ef15f9df3c.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $r=3p$\n\nII. $q=2t$\n\nIII. $s=-q$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. The vectors $r$ and $p$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $r$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $p$. So, $r\\ne 3p$.\n\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $q$ and $t$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $q$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $t$. So, $q\\ne 2t$.\n\n- Statement III is true. The vectors $s$ and $q$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $s$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $q$. So, $s=-q$.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Parallel Vectors From a Diagram"}]}
